# Implementation Plan — AETHER_MODEL Phase 4

## Objective
Execute **AETHER_MODEL Phase 4** to investigate and develop an Aether-owned neural model candidate while preserving the validated **Qwen2.5-1.5B-Instruct-Q4_K_M** GGUF baseline as the authoritative production inference engine. All work will follow strict evidence-driven principles: zero fabricated results, actual hardware limitation accounting, real execution of training/benchmarks, and preservation of platform compatibility.

---

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Hardware Boundary & Production Inference Retention:**
> The host system has an AMD Ryzen 3 3250U dual-core CPU with ~5.94 GB total RAM (with ~0.4–1.7 GB available free RAM) and no CUDA GPU.
> 1. Full fine-tuning or LoRA backpropagation on the 1.5B Qwen model is physically blocked on this hardware without fatal OS freeze / OOM.
> 2. The existing Track A custom transformer (~3.68M parameters) can be trained on the 218 Phase 3 records for deep-learning proof (loss decrease, backpropagation, optimizer updates, memorization), but cannot match a 1.5B-parameter model pretrained on trillions of tokens across general knowledge, reasoning, and tool formatting.
> 3. Therefore, `checkpoints/model.gguf` (Qwen2.5-1.5B-Instruct-Q4_K_M) will strictly remain the **authoritative production baseline**, and the Aether-native candidate will be evaluated as an **experimental candidate** under the model registry.

---

## Proposed Phases & Execution Steps

### 1. Forensic Audit & Baseline Preservation
- Confirm cryptographic integrity of `checkpoints/model.gguf` (SHA-256: `6a1a2eb6...`, size: 1,117,320,736 bytes).
- Verify all 38 existing tests pass (`test_phase2_production_baseline.py` 19/19, `test_phase3_adaptation_suite.py` 9/9, `test_phase3_evaluator_unit.py` 10/10).
- Audit directory structure and dependencies (`.venv` with `llama-cpp-python`, system Python with `torch`, `transformers`, `accelerate`).

### 2. Architecture & Tokenizer Verification
- **Tokenizer**: Run exhaustive roundtrip tests with `scripts/verify_phase4_tokenizer.py` across English, numbers, punctuation, Python/TS code, Unicode/emojis, and Indic languages (Hindi, Telugu, Tamil). Ensure all 9 special tokens are correctly mapped.
- **Track A Architecture**: Inspect embeddings, sinusoidal positional encoding, 6-layer 8-head multi-head attention, layer norm, GELU feed-forward, residual connections, causal masking, KV caching, and output head (~3.68M parameters).
- **Track B Specification**: Document architectural parameters, compute scaling, memory footprint, and token pretraining requirements for a 10M–50M compact decoder-only transformer.

### 3. Dataset & Contamination Verification
- Re-verify zero leakage across `data/phase3/` (`train.jsonl` 218 records, `val.jsonl` 36 records, `test.jsonl` 36 records) and the locked 105-prompt evaluation suite (`benchmark/phase3_evaluation_suite.json`).
- Ensure 0 exact, 0 normalized, and 0 near-duplicate overlaps.

### 4. Causal LM Loss & Tiny Overfit Proof
- **Loss Verification**: Run `scripts/verify_phase4_causal_loss.py` to mathematically verify causal next-token shift ($t_0..t_{N-1} \to t_1..t_N$, last token is `<eos>`), prompt and pad masking, numerical log-sum-exp stability, and finite-difference vs analytical gradient error (< 1e-5).
- **Tiny Overfit Test**: Execute `scripts/run_phase4_tiny_overfit.py` on 8 controlled samples over 35 epochs. Prove AdamW optimizer updates, monotonic loss reduction (>70%), checkpoint save/reload determinism (< 1e-6 logit diff), and auto-regressive generation.

### 5. Controlled Training Experiment (Track A)
- Train the Track A model on the complete 218 Phase 3 training records (`train.jsonl`) with validation evaluation on `val.jsonl` (36 records) using AdamW, cosine learning rate schedule, gradient clipping, and checkpointing.
- Track real metrics: step loss, epoch loss, validation loss, validation perplexity, token accuracy, elapsed time, peak RAM, CPU usage.
- Save deterministic checkpoint with full metadata and SHA-256 hash (`checkpoints/aether_checkpoint_phase4_candidate.json`).
- Perform checkpoint reload test to verify deterministic inference equivalence.

### 6. Locked 105-Prompt Benchmark & Comparison
- Evaluate the candidate model on the locked 105-prompt benchmark across all 14 categories (language quality, instruction following, arithmetic, reasoning, factual knowledge, conversation, summarization, JSON, tool formatting, multi-step, Aether identity, uncertainty, RAG/context, safe refusal).
- Construct honest category-by-category comparison table: Baseline (Qwen 1.5B GGUF) vs Candidate (Aether ~3.68M).
- Record latency, throughput (tok/s), memory, stability, and generation defects (repetition, premature EOS, syntax errors).

### 7. GGUF Export & llama.cpp Evaluation
- Evaluate GGUF export feasibility: assess custom NumPy tensor layout and non-standard 1024-token vocabulary compatibility with llama.cpp converter (`convert_hf_to_gguf.py`).
- Document conversion blockers or requirements for C++ architectural support.

### 8. Provider Compatibility & Model Registry
- Ensure `AETHER_BAC`'s `AetherModelProvider` and `AETHER_MODEL/aether/api/server.py` maintain model-independent contracts (`ILLMProvider` / `IModelProvider`: `/health`, `/model/status`, `/v1/models`, `/v1/generate`, `/v1/stream`).
- Create `checkpoints/model_registry.json` registering:
  - `qwen2.5-1.5b-instruct-q4km` (STATUS: VALIDATED BASELINE, Authoritative Default)
  - `aether-small-v0.1` (STATUS: EXPERIMENTAL CANDIDATE)

### 9. Platform Regression & Live Verification
- Run complete test regression in `AETHER_MODEL`: Phase 2 baseline (19 tests), Phase 3 adaptation (9 tests), Phase 3 evaluator (10 tests), and dedicated Phase 4 test suite.
- Run backend verification in `AETHER_BAC` to ensure orchestrator and provider compatibility.
- Live API verification: health checks, model status, generation, and streaming.

### 10. Final Report & Authoritative Verdict
- Author `AETHER_MODEL_PHASE4_REPORT.md` with all 25 mandated sections.
- Formulate the evidence-based final verdict:
  `AETHER MODEL PHASE 4 COMPLETE — TRAINING BLOCKED BY HARDWARE`
  (documenting what was attempted, what passed, what hardware was insufficient, future scaling path for 10M–7B, and retaining the validated Qwen GGUF baseline in production).

